      },
      "rationale": "Archer 2015 reports the 2014 national sample of 3,658. DeWitt 2016 explicitly reuses that national sample and index, but also analyses a distinct 2014-15 targeted sample of 6,861 from 18 schools. For the reused national sample, distribution and demographic results are repeat reporting, not a second independent dataset. However, DeWitt 2016 independently reports the same low/high distribution and South Asian/high-cultural-capital/top-set pattern in its targeted sample as well. Current Results explicitly attributes the younger-cohort distribution to BOTH papers, and Discussion explicitly places BOTH in the retested set. Its new 7,013-person survey measures the corresponding distribution and demographic pattern. Therefore the 2016 report is an empirically tested original paper, not merely the source of an instrument or an alternate title/version of the 2015 article. No claim is made that every 2016 analysis is retested. All supplied shipped counterparts and the root baseline have been checked: none represents this report.",
